The syntax and feature set of md, and the architecture of a Markdown editor that runs in the browser, were studied from
ThisIs-Developer/Markdown-Viewer (Apache License 2.0), https://github.com/ThisIs-Developer/Markdown-Viewer.
No code was copied from it.

md ships third-party packages under their own licences. Their names, versions and licences are listed in dist/trust.json,
written by `npm run build`, and the packages' licence files are in their own folders under node_modules/. The fonts in
public/fonts are Inter, JetBrains Mono, Literata and Newsreader, used under the SIL Open Font License; the licence text is public/fonts/OFL.txt.

md Local draws PlantUML diagrams with @plantuml/core (https://plantuml.com), MIT licence, Copyright (C) 2009-2024 Arnaud Roques.
Its licence text is node_modules/@plantuml/core/LICENSE. It bundles Viz.js (MIT, Copyright (c) Michael Daines), which contains Graphviz
and Expat. The C4 bundle in vendor/plantuml/ is C4-PlantUML 2.14.0 (MIT, Ricardo Niepel, kirchsth and contributors),
https://github.com/plantuml-stdlib/C4-PlantUML. These files ship in both editions, under /engine/, and load only when a document has such a diagram.

md Local draws draw.io diagrams with the draw.io viewer (viewer-static.min.js) from https://github.com/jgraph/drawio, release v32.6.9,
Apache License 2.0. Its licence text is the LICENSE file of that repository. The viewer includes mxGraph and other libraries that the project
states are all compatible with Apache 2.0. The stencil sets in vendor/drawio/stencils/ (aws4, azure, basic,
bpmn, cisco19, flowchart, gcp2, kubernetes) come from the same project's viewer and carry its stencil licence (src/main/webapp/stencils/LICENSE), which says:
"The icon sets and stencil libraries included in this software, and any derivatives thereof (including conversions to other formats, traced reproductions,
substantially similar visual representations, or AI-generated images created using these icons as reference or training input), may not be used as
software assets in, distributed for use with, or incorporated into Atlassian products or products distributed through the Atlassian marketplace or plugin
ecosystem, without explicit written permission. This restriction does not apply to end-user diagram output (such as exported images or documents)
created using this software." md is not an Atlassian product and must not be used as a software asset in one. These files ship in both editions, under /engine/, and load only when a document has such a diagram.

